## DJI Support

Existing DJI Action Camera Protocol Work

https://github.com/datagutt/node-osmo — The most relevant project

A TypeScript library that already reverse-engineered the BLE protocol for DJI Osmo Action 3/4/5 and
Pocket 3. It implements:

- BLE pairing
- WiFi connection triggering
- Resolution/FPS/bitrate/stabilizer control
- Battery percentage reading
- RTMP live streaming setup

It's early-stage (65 stars, 30 commits, stability issues acknowledged), but the protocol fundamentals
are decoded. The original reverse-engineering was done by someone credited as "Spillmaker".

https://github.com/eerimoq/moblin — iOS streaming app

A free iOS app that controls DJI Action cameras via BLE to start live streams. Tested with OA3, OA4,
and Pocket 3. It inspired node-osmo's implementation. No media download support though — it's
streaming-focused.

Other DJI reverse-engineering projects

- https://github.com/samuelsadok/dji_protocol — Partial documentation of DJI's proprietary protocols
(more drone-focused)
- https://github.com/vm32/Reverse-Engineering-DJI-drones — Toolkit for protocol analysis and firmware
exploration
- https://www.digidow.eu/publications/2021-christof-masterthesis/Christof_2021_MasterThesis_DJIProtoco
lReverseEngineering.pdf — Academic work on DJI WiFi protocol (drone-focused)

What's covered vs. what's missing
┌────────────────────────────┬────────────────────────────────────┐
│         Capability         │               Status               │
├────────────────────────────┼────────────────────────────────────┤
│ BLE discovery & pairing    │ Solved (node-osmo)                 │
├────────────────────────────┼────────────────────────────────────┤
│ WiFi AP activation via BLE │ Solved (node-osmo)                 │
├────────────────────────────┼────────────────────────────────────┤
│ Battery/status queries     │ Partially solved                   │
├────────────────────────────┼────────────────────────────────────┤
│ Camera settings control    │ Partially solved                   │
├────────────────────────────┼────────────────────────────────────┤
│ Media listing via WiFi     │ Unknown — not implemented anywhere │
├────────────────────────────┼────────────────────────────────────┤
│ Media download via WiFi    │ Unknown — not implemented anywhere │
└────────────────────────────┴────────────────────────────────────┘
Bottom line

The BLE control side is largely solved thanks to node-osmo — we'd be porting their TypeScript protocol
 knowledge to Go, not reverse-engineering from scratch. The big unknown is the WiFi/HTTP media layer —
 nobody seems to have reverse-engineered DJI's media list/download API yet. That would require
sniffing the DJI Mimo app's WiFi traffic to figure out how it lists and downloads files.

So the effort would be: ~30% porting known protocol, ~70% reverse-engineering the media/WiFi side
(unless DJI happens to use a standard protocol like FTP or a REST API on their WiFi AP, which would
make it much easier to discover).

Sources:
- https://github.com/datagutt/node-osmo
- https://github.com/eerimoq/moblin
- https://github.com/samuelsadok/dji_protocol
- https://github.com/vm32/Reverse-Engineering-DJI-drones
- https://www.digidow.eu/publications/2021-christof-masterthesis/Christof_2021_MasterThesis_DJIProtoco
lReverseEngineering.pdf